    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1050">

                <pb facs="0782" n="666" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg666"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.11/4674.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Brazilian Minister at Mexico
                            City to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Brazilian Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-06-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 8, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>52. In regard to Vice Consul Silliman I do not consider it advisable for him to
                    return to Saltillo for the present as I promised <pb facs="0783" n="667"
                        xml:id="pg667"/> to Department here that he would stay away from Mexico as
                    long as the present situation would last. The copies desired by Department are
                    being made and will be forwarded by mail in a day or two. Silliman was charged
                    with espionage although no concrete facts were mentioned as I understand. The
                    case seems to have been dismissed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cardoso de Oliveira</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
